  "id": "COMPOUND:9657 - PROTEIN:3968",
  "verbalization": "Famitinib is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase III subunit beta through a multi-step mechanism involving the thyroid hormone receptor alpha. The evidence suggests that Famitinib acts as a target for multiple compounds, including (3S)-N-(5-CHLORO-2-METHYLPHENYL)-1-CYCLOHEXYL-5-OXOPYRROLIDINE-3-CARBOXAMIDE, Pazufloxacin, and CP1-1189, all of which are known to target the thyroid hormone receptor alpha. These compounds, in turn, are linked to the DNA polymerase III subunit beta, indicating a potential pathway where the thyroid hormone receptor alpha serves as a mediator in the interaction between these agents and the DNA polymerase III subunit beta. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, mechanistically supported relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets for Famitinib implies a broader role in modulating cellular processes, potentially through the thyroid hormone receptor alpha, which could explain its effects on DNA polymerase III subunit beta.",
